{"BLOCK0": {"hash": "aca1b76b8851cbf9181957f57de43f0c0b2f7ffa8b02abb937303565bcb96515", "html": "Home Server / living infrastructure notebook", "inline": true}, "BLOCK1": {"hash": "142237f8704c623b6427cfe055303ffa428dff9b5db2583ba479f0c1b3a6364f", "html": "An old Mac mini became my private infrastructure platform.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK2": {"hash": "9c950bf49661daac01b3ea539a5ab4d7a9bc982c77a95bc8b4e8fa1ec3a8c8ab", "html": "What started as Ubuntu, Docker and SSH gradually became the control plane behind observability, networking, storage continuity, embedded-device work, sensing, environmental data and telephony R&amp;D.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK3": {"hash": "61da41feb5b4ed7a729618c8b9cfb60163587977bbc055478466ea9ea1682c1d", "html": "This page is intentionally not a finished case study. It is the canonical public place for the architecture, current state, active technical discussions and the decisions that keep changing the system.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK4": {"hash": "2f5d50add6260ef412c07aec72e73d423365250fa33e83e136c34443dd705961", "html": "Current status", "inline": true}, "BLOCK5": {"hash": "e0b48d59bd02f4eafd4ecbd44841a8761bf03b7f72b54b60a36ea7869cae172c", "html": "Living system, not a museum.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK6": {"hash": "a3b50c476732c7409d297c3d7d0e23569fee5e08318553ae76041ab5fe60582e", "html": "State", "inline": true}, "BLOCK7": {"hash": "00e00534612550123f46ab273938173eac53e273af044c8fdbdc3a1778252f1c", "html": "Ongoing engineering and R&amp;D platform.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK8": {"hash": "ef5b9ffbfd8c7a44c956b34f88d5dc951301f12d395da285b8a69916e61ae9e1", "html": "Core host", "inline": true}, "BLOCK9": {"hash": "55a5ca51e4319fef0c00cbb47de71ebdffdda4355a57a0f1c34e2caf2b5c3056", "html": "Older Mac mini running Ubuntu and containerized services.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK10": {"hash": "e8baefef21d1223d250894f44b96665f8ea6e5da6cc8aa8fbe484f53adf25e0f", "html": "Primary role", "inline": true}, "BLOCK11": {"hash": "f1ca5b2d47eca0c7a9d2c6caa7cc918e3f63c96c61dfaa76bb3ba19ac9d8c0a0", "html": "Stable coordination point for services, data, dashboards and remote operations.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK12": {"hash": "3a5ecca188c0579c00ee24cf3cab21bd02c15a06f7a70cc8e0a8ff2381dcbbfd", "html": "Updated", "inline": true}, "BLOCK13": {"hash": "754831c4697e2a0b4ad444baf2b5c0fcc04039d4ecbd4eaf80a8e27e8bc02056", "html": "25 Sep 2026", "inline": true}, "BLOCK14": {"hash": "b5fe6333f4031db128c5813e8923a10130b1b39ae721f5978a522cff9c34bc02", "html": "Why this page exists", "inline": true}, "BLOCK15": {"hash": "9733e6e21e0897ff239969b7144dfd09a0157696674cbe94acf11b220a79ab86", "html": "I did not start by designing a “homelab architecture.” Wi-Fi failed, so I needed recovery. Remote access mattered, so I needed a private network. Too many services appeared, so I needed observability. Too many dashboards appeared, so I needed a control surface. Devices started producing data, so the server became a data backend. Firmware and telephony work needed infrastructure, so they joined the same platform.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK16": {"hash": "9b6096141931fc2841169f534d4e812c9b51309ea662426a143b875baeae4fc6", "html": "The page therefore doubles as a living engineering notebook: when a homeserver discussion changes the architecture, creates a new operational rule, or closes an open problem, the durable result belongs here.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK17": {"hash": "160a7e25daa36375799762cff5759fb5535e3087228975b74bc7e920f2b042b3", "html": "Evolution", "inline": true}, "BLOCK18": {"hash": "2e95d0e2b97e84fc91ac2f3361db928ba66d801ed41d71b393f804c21074e284", "html": "Problems became architecture.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK19": {"hash": "bd9229d7af8af73896d470ee97136d2c6d962f2f2c4f51011189aff09a94fd48", "html": "An always-on Mac mini for containers, files, SSH access and experiments.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK20": {"hash": "91a6d4a3e844d651fb7804da49f83ae88e0971f976da60eac5f9299a71937e37", "html": "Broadcom Wi-Fi, routing and availability problems forced watchdog logic, NetworkManager recovery and a more explicit failure model.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK21": {"hash": "825ac33fcc2b4782a4f0bde909f00926957ac73e9415798be9ac8bf58f3f4153", "html": "Tailscale made the host a persistent private node. Cloudflare and Caddy separated controlled web ingress from private management paths.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK22": {"hash": "ee3b87c0bced98e8eb7413b1a9f40edcfadd8123a656ba1ba4093b100969d8ee", "html": "Desktop, laptop and hserver became nodes with different capabilities and availability. Workload placement and Nomad experiments followed.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK23": {"hash": "25f9c9bf43094e637fece3a9e198446e08af8e5a640fd8b32698d749a2604104", "html": "Prometheus and Grafana grew from host metrics into service state, network relationships, failure validation and operational evidence.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK24": {"hash": "ca2788449aea43aa977f9cee5c1f37d03b1b1a3dfc54844166bd97a43300c28b", "html": "Homarr, ingress, authentication, service-group controls and recovery views turned many independent tools into one operational surface.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK25": {"hash": "965a20100aedf87c9b88735afdb91f2e615ddc966518014327eba65f3e1afa44", "html": "Architecture now", "inline": true}, "BLOCK26": {"hash": "2d02cd3e125724c101f4ccdc93e005223de6f6409a91700ea10646c72a6065f1", "html": "Stable center, replaceable edges.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK27": {"hash": "b35df34a48fc6ea0118df9e3e896c2aacabb46cbe5ca0d032850b37e8b7687ff", "html": "Cloudflare for selected public services; Tailscale for private management and node-to-node reachability.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK28": {"hash": "d7d67b488532466798c70f812b674d04aa1ed424e73696d26a00add08fd5b2c1", "html": "Ubuntu, Docker, ingress, service coordination, operational dashboards, collectors and continuity services.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK29": {"hash": "6b9d3a312244c8a6631ce700c77353d58dc96f4ecf4987c7e16af55c2309c405", "html": "More capable machines can take heavier workloads while the home server remains the persistent coordination point.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK30": {"hash": "de058c7996d0ad1f76bacdd8cc82e1bc000c6beadee35e0a1bf37bc1b7da431e", "html": "Prometheus, Grafana, service state, logs and experiments around network-path visibility.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK31": {"hash": "d3f9572c96541ca061ae6448a1b9079a877317a73c42d96ecb2a5bdcf2c40c4e", "html": "Embedded firmware, OTA experiments, Wi-Fi CSI, GNSS/GSM and other physical-world telemetry.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK32": {"hash": "fc4eb5af8a5a8d801b20be75a33953614e6c03bc6cdc5883d50835f1d2d777e4", "html": "SIP/RTP infrastructure, environmental observatories, presence experiments and data services share the same underlying platform patterns.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK33": {"hash": "7e44ea30fc3941527fc8950db7c51230345b4824948a07867f29cb1e33a712e7", "html": "Current discussion threads", "inline": true}, "BLOCK34": {"hash": "7ceb226ed92d06cbcd0cdd527c23b2e631dcbf48fe246427add138c7a569a46f", "html": "What is still moving.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK35": {"hash": "925e5636720880589980ee7aecb6098e197b00544c7e5d4129a6bc2ab102a480", "html": "Chat-driven operations path", "inline": true}, "BLOCK36": {"hash": "2b23825ff9d84037d61b2859ad3d86c70aad8cf6408902ee38fed509accc961d", "html": "The weakest boundary is still AI/agent → MCP → hserver → other nodes. The work is around reliable access, authorization, auditability, safe execution and recovery when one machine disappears.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK37": {"hash": "742f282bcc5d815681d67a46aa013b8f87880c932da73d0260633f3521c4326b", "html": "Master operations surface", "inline": true}, "BLOCK38": {"hash": "0c24fa2ae68afc0f2d656eafca2ad393796663db014b95c29aaa29ec9ab13264", "html": "Homarr and Grafana are being consolidated so infrastructure, environmental data, presence/RF, telephony, storage and recovery remain discoverable from one place.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK39": {"hash": "82f75fc49ed6012a75b2e8ca1e14e72dbee4a731595e7613895e3cba318ad47a", "html": "Network observability", "inline": true}, "BLOCK40": {"hash": "ea549d47a4cc14daba1d62c56f95bcc84b037fa440ad30852191815374768dd0", "html": "Moving beyond container lists toward service groups, traffic relationships, timeline views, path tracing and better visibility into the whole LAN.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK41": {"hash": "f37a4abaddaf243ae6d811dc61674bfe7bc837835bf071742903eb01bd9c7a33", "html": "Service lifecycle control", "inline": true}, "BLOCK42": {"hash": "48ac61db4f8d16adad94f341b4ba351fe0a61af0afaa92c70fc4629344c98804", "html": "Heavy stacks should not run forever. Service-group toggles, maintenance windows and resource-aware operation are replacing permanent-on assumptions.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK43": {"hash": "3d88514991ce886b0e8559b11de159d1da822f0794338bfb7b85f9872a69da99", "html": "Sensor + CSI platform", "inline": true}, "BLOCK44": {"hash": "063c51489c6e356562889d4e28cab8bf9a963d6bedb5236e487411f5475fdc6f", "html": "Wi-Fi CSI, Android radio/GNSS data and calibration workflows are turning the server into a backend for physical-world sensing experiments.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK45": {"hash": "6f61bb1186c5b6c717482384633b94812d51ed316ef77462b34d29bc1be7bf29", "html": "Device + telephony infrastructure", "inline": true}, "BLOCK46": {"hash": "b726420f7b9cd20b1c51d152654c51b56c9224cb8800d44a4fd15ad8f41d3bc7", "html": "OTA fleet ideas, ESP32 development, SIP/RTP testing and PBX work continue to use the same server as a shared engineering lab.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK47": {"hash": "fd0a17ea32f2cc9b74c4670fb00f9e42c02d17c108f18197bc3016e27e801df9", "html": "What runs through it", "inline": true}, "BLOCK48": {"hash": "4beac9f6d6a46edb3cf69aec2dcaba957a4952d1d9ae671abc106d04eb3969d0", "html": "One platform, several engineering domains.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK49": {"hash": "ce0cff719a94747617230dde819ab25812021d6b80c236bf0c6891c0d46e45be", "html": "Infrastructure", "inline": true}, "BLOCK50": {"hash": "3194a11928648ca404306903f8e461f351a9cde01b1eb1ee9dda3669af4d425d", "html": "Linux hosts, Docker services, ingress, identity, service state and recovery.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK51": {"hash": "a37c93100e7c535c881a2a05767331145e0bcd4830543f6c1d84a0e10219b6bb", "html": "Observability", "inline": true}, "BLOCK52": {"hash": "d581bcca50b0d26937747400033a07772e0501046e6888fd2c2201b908e55de3", "html": "System metrics, dashboards, alert validation, service health and network behavior.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK53": {"hash": "fc6a07ab5b2fcb67a5855a1f463c4bf2451ccda5dc92a764b8fb49bbf8ce9076", "html": "Device infrastructure", "inline": true}, "BLOCK54": {"hash": "1c5723782be038fa8c633e80780e5674b52cfaacb6773f66842013a47e6c8336", "html": "Firmware lifecycle, provisioning, release states and embedded-device experiments.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK55": {"hash": "9c3113058c0aad91f41215b301320b5b7eace631c4fe3f87432d11425a9eca97", "html": "Sensing", "inline": true}, "BLOCK56": {"hash": "481c597ca8f0215dc3bd17127da3f2fdcbaccd335f6c6690afa6a0b807b7a2c1", "html": "Wi-Fi CSI, Android GNSS/GSM collection, calibration and time-series analysis.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK57": {"hash": "9e471951a1b4106e54be128a21112b02914fe98cc79b2c92b49ee80c5464487c", "html": "Environment", "inline": true}, "BLOCK58": {"hash": "d2e59bf026a206af6f10da177a441f97009ee32105195ebe34789b6c40dd982b", "html": "Weather, river, flood, satellite and other public-data integrations.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK59": {"hash": "9d6875ca6b884038ed7c3553fa9c994a40f9108f3784f406c20f251e38b7373d", "html": "Telephony", "inline": true}, "BLOCK60": {"hash": "2d68fdfcd4c7578fe4313d5458d247779a10fe5b740d45526fa89155e7ac9cdf", "html": "SIP signaling, RTP media, PBX integration, call-flow debugging and embedded voice.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK61": {"hash": "9d626095464802138dd461a4e9942d3b86e85d5c1ab43b68bd4e6ddbc494c598", "html": "Change log", "inline": true}, "BLOCK62": {"hash": "539f7d389075ea127c7c5248495267fc045d6e6a26bb57c94846939726cda2e0", "html": "Recent evolution.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK63": {"hash": "885aceb7c95008512240bcebb8dc2447facaf3f273c23ca4e86b037f46a7af6b", "html": "Consolidated operations around a master dashboard, Grafana hub, Caddy ingress and authentication instead of treating every dashboard as an isolated destination.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK64": {"hash": "0082935d3584345e9b94f2d9d40799f8f2f48565e254bc4ee3c6e08b6ddd6168", "html": "Expanded the server into an environmental and sensing backend: river/weather observatories, satellite integrations, Wi-Fi CSI and Android radio/GNSS collectors.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK65": {"hash": "e28dfe0dd19fe7eeb01a9fe00578606c336d512b15694eea451a8b2efd095dd8", "html": "Started treating expensive stacks as service groups with explicit on/off and maintenance behavior after resource and log-pressure problems exposed the cost of leaving everything running.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK66": {"hash": "bbfcdb7da081621de23015a3f530fff6f5c790a24cf9b1e9444ddc057c8eb773", "html": "Made OTA/device lifecycle and telephony labs part of the same infrastructure rather than separate one-off development environments.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK67": {"hash": "665ea8e8f4dd0725dd72b03cae7526c9f71a68d9915cd585091cdefde9f23650", "html": "Moved from local-only SSH toward Tailscale, watchdog recovery and remote operational access, changing the Mac mini from a nearby computer into a persistent infrastructure node.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK68": {"hash": "f38a3d19816caf9cea7b84ea8e0d0f2261bc7c3715f78126955e87179a2fadd0", "html": "Next engineering questions", "inline": true}, "BLOCK69": {"hash": "fd535e925f98feb8b8937302367f4074061d887f68d415b24085adfd1cceac3f", "html": "<span>01</span>How should machine selection and failover work when desktop, laptop or hserver disappears?", "inline": false}, "BLOCK70": {"hash": "18f718094e9b3436764ce4f8ac4df0ffa6b7fa500f8a56b6c534dbad37ceade4", "html": "<span>02</span>How much authority should a conversational operations layer have, and how should every action be auditable?", "inline": false}, "BLOCK71": {"hash": "17f2ff7407b22d4bef43838a593eb05786e25dd4f6f4ebe4482142cf8e964407", "html": "<span>03</span>Which data belongs in long-term storage versus short-lived experimental telemetry?", "inline": false}, "BLOCK72": {"hash": "d4690ae4f949284fac4b79eb28473caf590e0bed8521b1cc6274f9c486e0f909", "html": "<span>04</span>How do I keep the control plane understandable as more projects attach to it?", "inline": false}, "BLOCK73": {"hash": "eb832e655290e11659c9087280705d2d499df6e01a877114a737269fe43009dc", "html": "Working principle", "inline": true}, "BLOCK74": {"hash": "03901ef28fee665e519550116cfb6c364e1e18879db76e974517ae0644eb159a", "html": "Operate the system, not just the containers.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK75": {"hash": "b03025528a7468002d8b27f08ff9f6f94e1dd2a9c8b2963a9bc315d0ffdd4b48", "html": "The goal is not to collect self-hosted software. The goal is to make a small infrastructure environment explainable, recoverable and useful for real engineering work.", "inline": true}, "BLOCK76": {"hash": "602a91ff23f6af71f6d752c3b242a01d9a1c3ec8245403dbacb54ac4729da9e8", "html": "01 → 06", "inline": true}, "BLOCK77": {"hash": "938db8c9f82c8cb58d3f3ef4fd250036a48d26a712753d2fde5abd03a85cabf4", "html": "01", "inline": true}, "BLOCK78": {"hash": "a953f09a1b6b6725b81956e9ad0b1eb49e3ad40004c04307ef8af6246a054116", "html": "02", "inline": true}, "BLOCK79": {"hash": "0b8efa5a3bf104413a725c6ff0459a6be12b1fd33314cbb138745baf39504ae5", "html": "03", "inline": true}, "BLOCK80": {"hash": "6cd5b6e51936a442b973660c21553dd22bd72ddc8751132a943475288113b4c0", "html": "04", "inline": true}, "BLOCK81": {"hash": "c97550ce8213ef5cf6ed4ba48790c137df3ef6a5da20b48961001a634b6cead2", "html": "05", "inline": true}, "BLOCK82": {"hash": "aacd834b5cdc64a329e27649143406dd068306542988dfc250d6184745894849", "html": "06", "inline": true}, "BLOCK83": {"hash": "ec5ba0abb717da87aab2655bd4b4a40f93f2a591a0ade63611c42925c49c17e9", "html": "Access", "inline": true}, "BLOCK84": {"hash": "70ea1983c983deacc1b61805aea3d43648af